     The xxoo__sseett__wwrriitteerr() function allows custom “write” functions which can
     tailor how lliibbxxoo writes data.  An _o_p_a_q_u_e argument is recorded and passed
     back to the _w_r_i_t_e___f_u_n_c function, allowing the function to acquire context
     information.  The _c_l_o_s_e___f_u_n_c function can release this opaque data and
     any other resources as needed.  The _f_l_u_s_h___f_u_n_c function should flush any
     pending data associated with the opaque pointer.

